      "message": "something like this?\n\nPaused cpus are essentially cpus removed from running tasks or interrupts (unless they are pinned). Unpinned timers and hrtimers too are moved away. This allows the paused cpus to enter deep idle states thereby saving a lot of power. The exit from paused state is lightweight where a scheduling ipi is sent to the paused cpu and it come back up again.",
